.TH SWIZZLE 1 "June 2026" "swizzle 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
swizzle \- redirect file access paths for a program with LD_PRELOAD
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swizzle
.IR "[" SRC:DST " ...] -- " PROGRAM " [" ARG " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B swizzle
preloads
.B libswizzle.so
and runs
.IR PROGRAM ,
rewriting file access paths from each source prefix to its destination prefix.
.PP
Each
.I SRC:DST
mapping applies to
.I SRC
and paths below it. The longest matching source prefix wins when multiple
mappings match a path.
.PP
Relative paths in mappings are resolved against the current working directory
at process startup.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IR SRC:DST
Define a path mapping from source prefix
.I SRC
to destination prefix
.IR DST .
Zero or more mappings may be provided.
.TP
.B --
Separates mapping arguments from the command to execute.
.TP
.IR PROGRAM " [" ARG " ...]"
Program and arguments to execute with path rewriting enabled.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The wrapped program exited successfully.
.TP
.B 1
An internal setup error occurred (for example, failing to configure
.BR LD_PRELOAD ).
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line usage or malformed mapping.
.TP
.B 127
Failed to execute
.IR PROGRAM .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
swizzle foo:../common/foo bar/baz:/tmp/baaz -- myprogram --options
.fi
.PP
In this example, accesses to
.I foo
and
.I foo/...
are redirected to
.I ../common/foo
and
.IR ../common/foo/... ,
and accesses to
.I bar/baz
and
.I bar/baz/...
are redirected to
.I /tmp/baaz
and
.IR /tmp/baaz/... .
